b/id 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-92a47338-e5c2-507b-a67f-16316e526b27"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-92a47338-e5c2-507b-a67f-16316e526b27" :question/id #uuid "92a47338-e5c2-507b-a67f-16316e526b27" :question/math-academy-id "q-80821" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\lambda  \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -12)-2(-2-2\\lambda )+4(4+4\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+6{\\lambda }^{2}+15\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-6{\\lambda }^{2}-15\\lambda -8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $8:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 4,\\pm 8\n$$\n\n- Let's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}-6(1)^{2}-15(1)-8 & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Let's pick $x=-1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-15(-1)-8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-1$ is a root of the equation.\n\nSo, we can factor $(\\lambda +1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}-6{\\lambda }^{2}-15\\lambda -8$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $-6$ | $-15$ | $-8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-7$ | $-8$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +1)({\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda -8) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4b06b2ac-6eae-593d-9852-5522b16478ca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4b06b2ac-6eae-593d-9852-5522b16478ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b06b2ac-6eae-593d-9852-5522b16478ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f7df2b21-bb30-525d-9e2e-3424c69767ae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15237b61-8e4a-5f9d-a46d-f1c679f25f0b" "answer-b7d351e3-6f87-5e60-9b75-e0173bdd7a1f" "answer-efa5985d-1ed5-5b85-9d5e-b97611697302" "answer-f7df2b21-bb30-525d-9e2e-3424c69767ae" "answer-cd09c6e2-8436-5664-8cd9-04b180376a9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15237b61-8e4a-5f9d-a46d-f1c679f25f0b" :answer/id #uuid "15237b61-8e4a-5f9d-a46d-f1c679f25f0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,-2,4\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7d351e3-6f87-5e60-9b75-e0173bdd7a1f" :answer/id #uuid "b7d351e3-6f87-5e60-9b75-e0173bdd7a1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,1,-8\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efa5985d-1ed5-5b85-9d5e-b97611697302" :answer/id #uuid "efa5985d-1ed5-5b85-9d5e-b97611697302" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,2,4\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7df2b21-bb30-525d-9e2e-3424c69767ae" :answer/id #uuid "f7df2b21-bb30-525d-9e2e-3424c69