]} {:db/id 17592186078453 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d8a210d-995e-535a-9fa6-41cb0df374c0" "question-a7033116-7f31-505d-9b30-3f70773f08f3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d8a210d-995e-535a-9fa6-41cb0df374c0" :question/id #uuid "9d8a210d-995e-535a-9fa6-41cb0df374c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-69274" :question/problem "What is the value of $\\sqrt{1+81÷3}-(-8+3)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+81÷3}-(-8+3) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{1+81÷3}-(-5) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{1+27}+5 & = \\\\ \\sqrt{28}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we approximate the value of the radical using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{28}≈5‭.291\\,503\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we approximate the value of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{28}+5 & ≈ \\\\ ‭‭‭5.291\\,503+5 & = \\\\ 10.291\\,503 & ≈ \\\\ 10.292\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b57a9137-46c6-56a0-8684-2be92f313fab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b57a9137-46c6-56a0-8684-2be92f313fab" :answer-field/id #uuid "b57a9137-46c6-56a0-8684-2be92f313fab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95047847-b017-5a0b-95c7-067528cc8d44" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7c5aa268-63e4-5c47-9891-92a7d1698d23" "answer-74c48537-34b2-5ccf-ad5e-f4377afc1278" "answer-61738bb0-adff-576e-ab79-4270a837a4b7" "answer-95047847-b017-5a0b-95c7-067528cc8d44" "answer-42836e12-3199-5792-994a-293af74f2ed1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c5aa268-63e4-5c47-9891-92a7d1698d23" :answer/id #uui